# Chrome Extension Structure

Build Chrome extensions using Manifest V3 and TypeScript.

* Put the manifest and static assets in `public/`.
* Put background service-worker logic in `src/background/`.
* Put webpage-injected code in `src/content/`.
* Put popup and options interfaces in their respective folders.
* Keep Chrome API access, storage, messaging, and HTTP logic inside `src/services/`.
* Keep reusable UI in `src/components/`.
* Keep shared types and utilities separate.
* Do not mix UI, business logic, and Chrome API logic.
* Use message passing between background, content scripts, and extension pages.
* Request only necessary permissions.
* Never use remotely hosted executable code.
* Add new folders only when a feature clearly requires them.
